    {
      "id": 181110,
      "name": "Trajector",
      "username": "Trajector",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-08-12T18:30:25.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The destruction overrides the cards effect.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>So, essentially, I forgot to add an event which would interrupt all the effects that we were previously resolving: the card’s destruction. The destruction of the Construct interrupts its attempt to execute its on-damage effects, and then once it’s destroyed, it’s no longer there to do anything.</p>",
